Assessment guidance

•	 Students are expected to manufacture at least one basic production aid.  Any

appropriate material can be used for to manufacture this items, including card or a thin
sheet of polymer.  The process used could be manual, such as scissors, craft knives or
similar and the processes used can be either CNC or manually controlled.

•	 You must make a note on the Unit Recording Sheet (URS) of any assistance students

required to accurately measure, mark out and cut out templates.

•	 You should ensure that students have the opportunity to carry out relevant supporting
research for the operating parameters of the equipment – this might be achieved by
access to manufacturers manuals or the internet.

•	 Please remind students about the requirement to reference all sources.

•	 Any appropriate formats can be used for the standard operating procedure.
•	 Students should be able to use a provided drawing to create a working drawing with

sufficient information for the CNC manufacturing operation.

•	 Evidence must include copies of the CAD drawings, the instructions or program created
by the CAD software for the CNC machine, and screenshots of the on-screen simulation
and data transfer.

•	 The on-screen simulation can be carried out using a separate CAD software package or
an animation of the operation. If an on-screen simulation is not available students can
evidence this task with a video of a practice operation.

•	 Students are required to set up and operate a CNC process/equipment. OCR does not
specify the manufacturing process/equipment to use for the set assignment, but the
minimum resource requirement is to have access to 3D printers and laser cutters.

•	 Evidence could be collated in the form of a practical diary, that contains annotated

photographs. This should be completed individually, so it would be highly unusual to
see the same output from all students in a cohort.

