Aims

There is often a need to manufacture one-off products
in engineering.  This might be for a unique application
or product, or there may be a need to manufacture
replacements for failed items.  In addition, there will
often be the need to produce a prototype in order to
evaluate a design.

a product in small quantities.  You will also learn how
to select and safely use the equipment, processes and
tools required to mark out, measure and manufacture
a product in small quantities, using a range of hand-
held equipment and conventional (non-Computer
Numerical Control (CNC) machining methods.

In this unit you will learn to identify the information
required to make a product, plan the production
of a product and carry out risk assessments for the
processes, tools and equipment needed to produce

